BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack-O-Lantern Spectacular
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
DTSTAMP:20261028T164839Z
UID:a11cb847b167f6db3762e7d7aba4@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Jack-O-Lantern Spectacular: The Great Pun-Kin Trail\, presente
 d by Citizens\, returns October 1 &#8211\; November 1 with an all-new trai
 l of clever carvings guaranteed to make you smile\, groan\, and laugh out 
 loud. This year’s theme celebrates the art of the pun\, with thousands o
 f hand-carved pumpkins bringing witty wordplay to life through pop culture
  references\, playful characters and pun-believable scenes. From clever on
 e-liners to delightfully cheesy dad jokes\, there’s something to make ev
 ery guest grin as they stroll The Great Pun-Kin Trail\, where over 5\,000 
 glowing jack-o’-lanterns illuminate the Zoo. Don’t miss New England’
 s “must-see” family-friendly event of the Halloween season at Roger Wi
 lliams Park Zoo. All tickets must be purchased online in advance. Tickets 
 are required and sold online only. No refunds or rescheduling. Buy Tickets
 \n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/jack-o-lantern-spectacu
 lar/92071/
LOCATION:Roger Williams Park Zoo\, 1000 Elmwood Avenue\, Providence\, RI 0
 2907
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/jack-o-lantern-spectacular/9207
 1/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coastal Cruisers Fall Foliage Tours (+ Cider & Donuts)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
DTSTAMP:20261028T164839Z
UID:6d1f100e0388a1db3baa480bef75@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Coastal Cruisers Fall Foliage Tours (+ Cider &amp\; Donuts) Ex
 perience Newport at its most beautiful on our 2-hour Fall Foliage Tour. Tr
 avel along historic Bellevue Avenue\, past iconic estates\, and through sc
 enic\, tree-lined backroads showcasing classic New England fall colors. Yo
 ur local guide will share Newport’s history while taking you beyond the 
 traditional tourist routes\, with scenic stops for photos along the way. T
 o complete the fall experience\, enjoy complimentary apple cider and fresh
  apple cider donuts while taking in the crisp autumn air and beautiful New
 port scenery. 🍎🍩 What's Included Apple Cider and Donuts Itinerary Hi
 storic Bellevue Avenue: Cruise past Newport’s famous Gilded Age mansions
  surrounded by beautiful fall colors. Newport’s Scenic Backroads: Leave 
 the traditional tourist route and explore quiet\, tree-lined roads\, histo
 ric stone walls\, and classic New England scenery. Newport Country Club &a
 mp\; Ocean Drive Area: Travel through some of Newport’s most picturesque
  areas\, with sweeping landscapes and seasonal foliage. Scenic Photo Stops
 : Stop at select locations along the way for photos and time to take in th
 e fall scenery. Return Through Historic Newport: Finish the experience wit
 h more Newport history and views as we make our way back. Highlights 🍂 
 Newport’s Best Fall Scenery: Experience colorful tree-lined roads\, hist
 oric stone walls\, and classic New England landscapes. 🏛️ Gilded Age 
 Newport: Travel along Bellevue Avenue and see Newport’s iconic mansions 
 surrounded by autumn colors. 🌳 Beyond the Traditional Tour Route: Explo
 re quieter backroads and scenic areas near Newport Country Club that many 
 visitors never see. 📸 Picture-Perfect Stops: Enjoy opportunities to ste
 p out\, take photos\, and experience Newport during its most colorful seas
 on.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/coastal-cruisers-fal
 l-foliage-tours-(%2b-cider-%26-donuts)/112431/
LOCATION:Coastal Cruisers\, 478 Thames Street\, Newport\, RI 02840
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/coastal-cruisers-fall-foliage-t
 ours-(%2b-cider-%26-donuts)/112431/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A New England Thanksgiving
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261028
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261029
DTSTAMP:20261028T164839Z
UID:c920b700ee6b0297b2c41185dc19@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Join the Coggeshall staff as we prepare a Thanksgiving meal ov
 er the hearth in our historic farmhouse. The late 18th century was before 
 the official start of Thanksgiving as a national holiday\, but the day was
  still celebrated with food and prayer in New England. Watch our costumed 
 historians make chicken on a string\, bake a pie in the hot coals\, mash t
 urnips and churn butter. In the woodshop we will also demonstrate carving 
 wooden spoons. Explore the garden to see the last of the fall harvest. Wal
 k the nature trail and look for signs of wild turkey\, see musket demonstr
 ations and try your aim with rubber band targets. Please note: This is not
  a Thanksgiving meal for visitors to eat. Food prepared in the historic Fa
 rmhouse Kitchen does not meet modern health and food preparation codes for
  public consumption.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/a-n
 ew-england-thanksgiving/112116/
LOCATION:Coggeshall Farm Museum\, 1 Colt Drive\, Bristol\, 02809 Time: 10:
 00 AM to 4:00 PM
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/a-new-england-thanksgiving/1121
 16/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:American Gothic: Dark Stories for a Young Nation
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261028
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261029
DTSTAMP:20261028T164839Z
UID:c98a0bb5cd7a807c82e1890d460b@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:As our commemoration of the 250th continues\, join us on Wedne
 sday\, October 28th at 6 pm for “American Gothic: Dark Stories for a You
 ng Nation” as we explore some of America’s best-known dark literature 
 and its New England roots. Together with Brown University English Professo
 r Jim Egan\, we will examine the literary and historical contexts behind c
 lassic 19th-century stories by essential American authors Washington Irvin
 g\, Nathaniel Hawthorne\, and Edgar Allan Poe. We will also be joined by r
 etired National Park Ranger John McNiff\, who will help to bring this genr
 e to life by reading selections from “The Legend of Sleepy Hollow\,” 
 “Young Goodman Brown\,” and the entirety of “The Tell-Tale Heart.”
  The program begins at 6 pm. Guests may arrive at 5:30pm for a wine and ch
 eese reception. Egan is a Professor of English at Brown University. He spe
 cializes in 17th- and 18th-century colonial British-American literature\, 
 and he studies various aspects of the role of literature in an information
  age. Guests can register here. Tickets are $10 for RIHS members and $15 f
 or non-members.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/american
 -gothic%3a-dark-stories-for-a-young-nation/112021/
LOCATION:Rhode Island Historical Society\, Aldrich House\, 110 Benevolent 
 Street\, Providence\, RI 02906
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/american-gothic%3a-dark-stories
 -for-a-young-nation/112021/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Aperitivo! Wines of New Zealand
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261028
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261029
DTSTAMP:20261028T164839Z
UID:54150adc73da782d3247e600f5ed@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Center for Wine and Culinary Arts at Ocean Hous
 e for a delightful Aperitivo Class featuring the unique wines and flavors 
 of New Zealand. In this immersive class\, our expert sommelier will guide 
 you through a selection of wines. Each wine will be thoughtfully paired wi
 th small bites. The expertly crafted pairings will perfectly complement th
 e bold\, nuanced flavors of the wines\, offering a true taste of New Zeala
 nd. Whether you’re looking to deepen your knowledge of wines or simply e
 njoy an evening of delicious pairings and conversation\, this Aperitivo Cl
 ass promises to be a memorable experience. Reservations are recommended\, 
 as space is limited. Please note: Tickets purchased for this event are non
 -refundable.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/aperitivo!-
 wines-of-new-zealand/112369/
LOCATION:Ocean House\, 1 Bluff Avenue\, Westerly\, 02891 Time: 5:30 PM to 
 10:30 PM
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/aperitivo!-wines-of-new-zealand
 /112369/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Santa Magic in Long Wharf
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261028
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261029
DTSTAMP:20261028T164839Z
UID:28ac69b35762d2d3f0b55bd51999@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:🎄✨ Holiday Tree Lighting Event!✨🎄 Mark your calendar
 s! The holiday season is kicking off at the Shops of Long Wharf\, and you 
 won’t want to miss it! 🎅🎁 📅 When: Saturday\, November 28th Rain
  Date: Sunday\, November 29th ⏰ Time: 4:00 PM &#8211\; 6:00 PM 📍 Wher
 e: The Shops of Long Wharf\, Newport 💰 Cost: Free to attend Bring the w
 hole family down for an afternoon packed with festive holiday magic and co
 mpletely FREE activities: 📸 Pictures with Santa and his elves! 🎶 Fes
 tive holiday music! 🎨 Fun kid crafts right here at Cutie Curls! ✍️ 
 Letters to Santa station! 🖌️ Free face painting! A huge thank you to 
 our co-sponsors\, Cutie Curls\, Newport In Bloom and the Shops of Long Wha
 rf\, for helping us bring this holiday cheer to the community! ❤️ Gath
 er the kids\, bundle up\, and come make some wonderful holiday memories wi
 th us. We can't wait to see you all.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisla
 nd.com/event/santa-magic-in-long-wharf/112462/
LOCATION:Long Wharf Mall\, 49 Long Wharf Mall\, Newport\, RI 02840
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/santa-magic-in-long-wharf/11246
 2/
END:VEVENT
